mutant: m083_import_accepts_unregistered_hole
target: internal/catalog/migration_scripts.go
failure-mode: |
  An import accepts a block that starts past the catalog's frontier with no
  registered vacancy bridging the hole. A source that lost a block, or a
  migrator that skipped one, imports a seq range nobody can read, and the
  pods' readers fail or skip events instead of the import failing loudly.
expected-detection: |
  TestMigration_ImportRefusesHoles imports blocks across unregistered holes
  between and inside segments and before active blocks, and requires
  migration corruption with nothing committed.
expected-tier: migration
tiers: migration

